<title>RUSSIA: Death toll from Russian LUKoil-unit blast rises.</title>
<headline>Death toll from Russian LUKoil-unit blast rises.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people killed by an explosion at a building used by a unit of LUKoil, Russia's largest oil producer, has risen to 18, a LUKoil statement received on Wednesday said.</p>
<p>It said more than 30 people had suffered as a result of the blast, caused by a kitchen gas canister at the main administrative building of LUKoil-Permneft, near the town of Kueda, 250 km (155 miles) south of the Urals city of Perm.</p>
<p>The explosion took place on Monday in the canteen of the two-storey building during a workers' meeting.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
